<Base title="Thanks | Storya Consulting" description="Your answers have been received." path="/start/thanks" noindex>
<div class="pagehead">
    <p class="eyebrow">Received</p>
    <h1>Thanks, <em>we've got it.</em></h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>One of us will read your answers and write back within one working day. While you wait, here is something you can use on Monday without us.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="doc" aria-label="Data line template preview">
    <p class="doc__kicker">One-page template</p>
    <h2>The data line: what may go into which tool</h2>
    <p>A written rule short enough that people follow it. The suggested starting point is in each cell. Change it to fit your firm, then write down who owns it.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Public chatbot, personal or free account</th><th>Firm-licensed AI tool</th><th>Tool built on your own accounts</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Published material: articles, released statements</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Your own drafts and internal notes</td><td>Avoid</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Client material not yet public: embargoed announcements, results</td><td>No</td><td>Only with a named person's sign-off</td><td>Yes, if built so it can't reach a public model</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Personal data: names and contact details of journalists, executives, clients' staff</td><td>No</td><td>Only what the task needs</td><td>Only what the task needs</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Client financials, deal terms, anything under NDA</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Only with the client's written agreement</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p><strong>Who owns this rule:</strong> ______________ <strong>Reviewed:</strong> ____________ <strong>Where it is written down:</strong> ______________</p>
    <p class="fine"><strong>Why write it down.</strong> Singapore's PDPC issued advisory guidelines on personal data in generative AI on 20 July 2026. They say organisations that use these systems under their authority bear primary responsibility for what goes into them, and encourage clear written policies. The guidelines are advisory. The PDPA they interpret is law. This template is not legal advice and is not a compliance certification.</p>
    <p class="fine">Storya Consulting · storyaconsulting.com</p>
    <div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="/storya-data-line-template.pdf" download>Download the PDF</a><span class="cta-row__aside">One page, A4, ready to print.</span></div>
  </article>

  <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top:2.4rem">
    <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/">Back to the site</a>
    <a class="linkcap" href="/#videos">Watch the series</a>
  </div>
</Base>
